# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Citation File Format (CFF) 1.2.0 — Swarmbly AI (integrated distribution)
#
# This repository is the umbrella of Swarmbly AI: SwarmblyCore (in-tree),
# SwarmblyLCE and SwarmblyApp (mirrors). Each component has its own DOI,
# listed under `identifiers`; cite the component you used and, for the design
# argument, the whitepaper (`preferred-citation`). The DOI of distribution
# 3.0.0 is minted by Zenodo at release and added here afterwards: an invalid
# DOI in a published citation record is worse than an absent one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Swarmbly AI in academic work, please cite the component(s) you
  used (DOIs below) and the whitepaper (see `preferred-citation`).
type: software

title: "Swarmbly AI"
abstract: >-
  Swarmbly AI is a decentralized, local-first AI system that splits the
  problem rather than the model. A local orchestrator keeps personal and
  sensitive work on the user's computer and sends public, decomposable work
  once to volunteer nodes running complete small language models, assembling
  the answer locally. This repository is the integrated distribution of its
  three components: SwarmblyCore (protocol, specification, reference
  implementation, measurement harness and benchmark), SwarmblyLCE (the Local
  Cognitive Extension, a memory that lives only on the user's device) and
  SwarmblyApp (the desktop client, peer-to-peer node and network monitor),
  with an interactive installer for macOS, Linux and Windows. Alpha software;
  measurements and their limits are stated in each component.

